/* ==========================================================================
   Hero Stories: "Someone I Don't Know" as a hand-written picture book.
   Same story as the Hero Movie (videos/stranger-safety-cinematic/script/
   script.json): a windy kite day at Sunny Meadow Park with Alex, Dad and
   Nutty; a grown-up Alex doesn't know (a goat) picks up the kite, offers
   candy, then asks Alex to come see a puppy in the car; Alex stays back where
   Dad can see, says no, runs to Dad and tells him; Captain Caution gives the
   tip. The book tells it in more detail at the higher levels.

   Read by js/page-storybook.js. Format (all text is { en, es }):
     scenes    picture id -> { file, shows (painter brief), alt }
               files live in img/book/<topic>/. Scenes are shared by levels.
     cover     scene id for the front cover picture
     levels[n] one book per level (0 = Pre-K–K, 1 = grades 1–3, 2 = grade 4+)
       pages      [{ id, pic, en:[paragraphs], es:[paragraphs] }]
       questions  asked inside the book, right after page `after`.
                  kind: recall | sequence | feeling | cause | vocab | predict | infer | theme
                  look: the page that holds the answer ("Look back at page N")
                  reveal (predict only): the page that shows what happens
                  choices: [{ en, es, ok, icon }] (predict: `clue` marks the
                  guess the story gives clues for; every guess is welcome)
                  hint: kind nudge after a wrong answer (the page number is
                  added for you); why: said after the right answer
                  then: optional second part ("How do you know?")
       recap      the 2 end-of-book Super Reader questions (same format)
       learned    the "What we learned" list on the last page
   Text may use {page:<page id>} for that page's number in the book.
   Never use he/she for Alex (the learner's own name can replace "Alex").
   Tools: node tools/build-book-briefs.js writes the picture briefs.
   ========================================================================== */
